🔹 2. Static Nested Class
✅ Definition:
A class defined inside another class with the static keyword.

✅ Characteristics:
Can only access static members of the outer class directly.

Can be instantiated without an instance of the outer class.

✅ Use Case:
Used for grouping classes that are only used in one place and don't need access to instance-level members.

▶️ Example:
java
Copy
Edit
public class OuterClass {
    private static String staticMessage = "Hello from static";

    // Static nested class
    static class StaticNestedClass {
        void printMessage() {
            System.out.println("Message: " + staticMessage);
        }
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        OuterClass.StaticNestedClass nested = new OuterClass.StaticNestedClass();
        nested.printMessage();
    }
}
