🔍 Comparison Summary:
| Feature                        | Non-Static Inner Class       | Static Nested Class        |
| ------------------------------ | ---------------------------- | -------------------------- |
| Belongs to                     | Instance of outer class      | Class itself               |
| Can access outer instance vars | ✅ Yes                        | ❌ No (only static members) |
| Requires outer class instance  | ✅ Yes                        | ❌ No                       |
| Use case                       | When inner class needs outer | Utility/helper classes     |


🧠 Real-World Use Cases:
Non-Static Inner Class:
java
Copy
Edit
class Car {
    private String engineType = "V8";

    class Engine {
        void showEngine() {
            System.out.println("Engine: " + engineType);
        }
    }
}
Used when the inner object (Engine) is tightly coupled with outer object (Car).

